    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, headlined by a massive 76.11 score for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Despite hitting eighth, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a priority start against Fedde; the favorable matchup against a 5.37 xERA starter, combined with his elite sprint speed and a high-probability stolen base opportunity against a slow delivery, makes him our highest-upside asset. **Christian Yelich** (71.71) and **Carson Benge** (67.24) also provide strong value, with **Carson Benge** benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against E. Rodr\u00edguez and **Christian Yelich** capitalizing on a prime #4 lineup slot. **Junior Caminero** (61.60) rounds out our elite-tier options, finding a favorable path to production against the matchup-appropriate pitching of E. P\u00e9rez.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully against the elite arm of Skenes, which dampens the outlook for both **Trea Turner** (49.79) and **Kyle Schwarber** (48.24). While their talent floors remain high, the significant skill of the opposing starter mandates tempered expectations for their daily efficiency. Our toughest bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (44.49), who sits just outside the active roster; despite a solid enough projection, he was nudged out by the superior categorical upside of our starters who offer more significant speed and platoon advantages. We are monitoring **Luke Raley**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Hyeseong Kim** closely as their lineup positions are currently pending; should their confirmed batting orders drift toward the bottom of the lineup, their efficiency scores\u2014already hovering near the marginal threshold\u2014could see further downward volatility. While the weather reports show some wind interference, the primary risk to our daily output remains the caliber of the starting pitching on the other side of the diamond.",
